The National Institute for Research & Development in Informatics represents the most important Institute for research, development and innovation in Information Technology and Communications in Romania. 
Areas of expertise
• communication networks and advanced technologies for application development in shared environments;
• information and communication technologies in areas of public interest;
• digital content, creativity and personal development;
• information and communication technologies, base for development of business and industry; new models and technologies in Systems and Software Engineering;
• knowledge-based systems, learning and cognitive systems;
• advanced systems for calculations and automated control.

The IDA (Industrial Development Agency) is a state-owned, join-stock company under ownership supervision of the Chancellery of the Prime Minister of Poland. The IDA supports business enterprises in operation and development of business activity, as well as in the implementation of restructuring processes, and plays a major role in increasing competitiveness of Polish industry. The broad spectrum of support instruments includes both financial products and non-financial assistance in implementation of projects, such as providing access to investment areas and production facilities within Special Economic Zones administered by the IDA. The Company also makes it possible for business partners to liaise in implementing innovative projects. As part of the Polish Development Fund Group, the IDA cooperates with major Polish institutions supporting enterprises and provides comprehensive solutions in response to the current needs and challenges faced by businesses.
Since 2016, IDA has been conducting a dedicated support program for Polish space companies: &ldquo;Comprehensive support program for Polish space technology sector&rdquo;. This program defines and divides all IDA activities in four fields:
&bull;Human Resources development;
&bull;New business projects;
&bull;Promotion;
&bull;Financial instruments.
In each defined field IDA has developed support mechanism. Since 2016 each year IDA together with Polish Space Industry Association organises internship program. Up to 15 companies can hire an intern chosen in a contest for six months, IDA covers up to 50% of costs of such internship. During three finished editions, all together 43 young specialist were hired by 21 companies. IDA has also started initiative Space Academy, which main idea is to enable young engineers retrain from other speciality to space technology sector. Using competences of Warsaw University of Technology, Military University of Technology and Space Research Centre Polish Academy of Science training focused on Satellite Integration Phases &ndash; 0/A/B/C/D is offered with partial financing of IDA. 
IDA supports national programs dedicated to start-up acceleration, one of them is European Satellite Navigation Competition 2016, Space3ac Acceleration Program 2016 or European Rover Challenge 2018. Recently IDA become partner of MyGalileoApp competition of European Global Navigation Satellite System Agency. Additionally to improve cooperation between Polish large companies and SME&rsquo;s, IDA provides service in searching and selecting innovative project for large companies in specified fields. Such activity/contest is done together with industrial partners and it&rsquo;s called ARP Innovation Pitch. Since 2016 we have organised 20 such contests. One of ARP Innovation Pitch was dedicated to space technology.
Activities of IDA related with international promotion are: financial support of national stand on international conferences and trades: Paris Space Week 2016, SpaceTech Expo 2017 (Bremen) or International Astronomical Congress 2018 (Bremen). National promotion is implemented by organising large events: Satellite Forum 2017, European Space TechTransfer Forum 2019 or supporting existing ones: Space Sectore Forum (2016 and 2018). Since 2017 IDA has launched dedicated loan program for polish space companies. One of the financial support mechanisms is the Open Innovation Network project that involves animating and supporting technology transfer transactions to Polish SMEs sector. Enterprises can obtain the grants which refund up to 70% of costs invested in the purchase of innovative technologies. Project is financed form UE founds. IDA is active both Polish space technology sector and generally technology transfer. IDA has dedicated platform for technology transfer between polish companies: Technology Transfer Platform.
